{
  "_doc": "The Atlas Vault item rules (packages/shared/src/vault.ts, crates/atlas-client/src/vault.rs), asserted by both. Every value is a field of a `vault.item` entity, end-to-end encrypted (manifests/vault.json keeps none plaintext). `create`: `input` (the keys type, name, fields, urls, notes, tags, folder, favorite) at `now` gives the stored `fields`, or fails with `error` {code, message}. `update`: a stored `item` and a `patch` (the create keys, `folder: null` clears; or `set_fields`/`remove_fields` instead of `fields`) at `now` give the `changes` written (field → value; none when nothing changed), or an `error`. A changed or removed secret field (kind hidden or totp) leaves its old value in `history`, newest first, at most 5 per field name. `read`: raw stored `fields` (another client's, possibly malformed) read as `item` and listed as `summary` (no field values). `resolve`: a reference (id, or name case-insensitively among items outside the trash) among `items` gives an `id` or an `error`. `field`: one field's value by name, case-insensitively.",
